  "plain": "Weather records from 2004 show an extremely strong wind out of the north at the height of the object in FLIR1, an infrared video a Navy jet filmed off Southern California, which the story ties to a white oval object shaped like a Tic Tac mint. Marik von Rennenkampff raises the point during a debate about the footage, crediting the analysis to someone named Yannick. The wind matters because it would decide whether the object could have been a balloon simply drifting with the air."
